I've completed the architectural-fit review of chunk c2 (`form_handler.gleam` + `questions.gleam`) and written the finding to `/Users/moses/code/_bmad-output/perkins/righttenantry-refcheck-rc3-3/r2/architecture-c2.json`.

**Summary of what I verified against the codebase:**

- **Import graph is a clean DAG** — `form_copy` (leaf) → `questions` → `form_pages`/`form_question_pages` → `form_handler`; no circular dependencies; `questions` correctly does not import back into the handler/view layer.
- **Module boundaries respected** — `questions.gleam` is pure data + pure functions (registry, validation, read-back) per spec decision 1's "single source of truth"; `form_handler` is HTTP orchestration; views delegate rendering. The `classify`/`classify_row`/`lookup_context` split mirrors the `dsar_handler` precedent (typed `LookupError`).
- **Reuse claims check out** — `application_handler.is_honeypot_filled`, `form_view.current_unix_ms`, `send.send_invite`/`SendDeps`/`RefereeContext`, `messages.first_name`/`channel_name`/`outcome_name` all exist as pub fns and are used as documented.
- **Deliberately-rejected items NOT re-litigated** — `thousands_separated` (duplicates private `ai/evidence_humanize.with_thousands_separator`) and the `is_timing_suspicious_within` reimplementation (decision 12's 500ms/11-day adaptation) are both explicitly justified in the spec; per the lens-guard I did not re-raise them.

**One note raised:** `form_handler.get_value` (line 876) is a near-duplicate of the already-imported `application_handler.get_form_value` (line 2319), differing only in that the local copy omits `string.trim`. Unnecessary duplication with a subtle semantic fork.
